[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_missdef")
id = &"mutaha_1_blocks"
display_name = "Mutaha"
briefing = "A city on a fork in the river, and everything worth taking is on the island in the middle of it. You come in from the south, 300 metres of open ground, and then it is streets: 7 metres wide, block after block, with the two districts either side of the water and six bridges between them. The riverbed is not wadeable. Those six crossings are the whole map.

The island is the spine and the campus is the prize — the gatehouse at the south end, the server garden in the middle, and the data hall itself, which is fifteen seconds at a console with both banks free to come back over the bridges at you. Clock Square across the west bridge is held in strength and the fairground in the east feeds chasers into the streets from a hive under the wheel.

New in this city: marksmen on the long streets — one shot, slowly, from further out than anything else they field, and they will not fire inside twelve metres. Rovers with grenade launchers that do not need to see you to put three rounds where you are. And a mortar track parked two streets back, shelling whatever its infantry can see. Their listening post on the north island is what feeds the long guns; take it down and they shoot on their own eyes.

Take the gatehouse, the server garden, the data hall and Clock Square, then get the squad out north on the river road."
level_scene = ExtResource("3_mutaha")
map_position = Vector2(500, -60)
